# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER COMMIT: the résumé.
# It carries a phone number, an email address and a home address. The site is
# built to stand on its own without it — LinkedIn is the contact channel.
# The file normally lives one level up, outside this repo. These rules are the
# second line of defence in case a copy ever lands inside it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pdf
*.doc
*.docx
*Resume*
*resume*
*CV*
*Cover*Letter*

# NEVER COMMIT: original photos.
# The originals carry EXIF GPS coordinates from where they were taken, several
# of them at home. Only the processed, metadata-stripped copies in
# assets/img/gallery/ belong in git. Rebuild them with:
#     python3 tools/process_photos.py
photo/
photos/
originals/
*.HEIC
*.heic
*.HEIF
*.heif
*.DNG
*.dng
*.CR2
*.NEF
*.ARW
*.MOV
*.mov
*.MP4
*.mp4
*.AAE

# Keep the built gallery: it is intentionally committed so GitHub Pages can
# serve the site with no build step. Re-allow anything the rules above caught.
!assets/img/**/*.jpg
!assets/img/**/*.webp
!assets/img/**/*.png
!assets/img/**/*.svg

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Editors & tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/

# Scratch
_preview_tmp/
_rev/
tmp/
*.log
